  "evidencia": "Page: Seven Faces. Sentence: Based upon the piece of short fiction \"A Friend of Napoleon\" which was published in the June 30, 1923, issue of \"The Saturday Evening Post\" magazine by popular writer Richard Connell (whose best known work, \"The Most Dangerous Game\", was filmed three years later), it was directed by Berthold Viertel and stars Paul Muni in his second screen appearance.\nPage: The Most Dangerous Game. Sentence: \"The Most Dangerous Game\", also published as \"The Hounds of Zaroff\", is a short story by Richard Connell, first published in \"Collier's\" on January 19, 1924.",
