        "original_id": "dfa25a10-0b05-501c-be01-953aa75ae177",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Seven Faces, A Friend of Napoleon, The Most Dangerous Game, The Hounds of Zaroff\n- People: Richard Connell, Berthold Viertel, Paul Muni\n- Publications: The Saturday Evening Post, Collier's\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Connell's short fiction \"A Friend of Napoleon\" was published in The Saturday Evening Post on June 30, 1923.\n- Richard Connell's short story \"The Most Dangerous Game,\" also published as \"The Hounds of Zaroff,\" was first published in Collier's on January 19, 1924.\n- Richard Connell's best-known work is \"The Most Dangerous Game.\"\n- \"The Most Dangerous Game\" was filmed three years after its publication.\n- The film \"Seven Faces\" was based on Richard Connell's \"A Friend of Napoleon.\"\n- Berthold Viertel directed \"Seven Faces.\"\n- Paul Muni starred in \"Seven Faces\" in his second screen appearance.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
